      <h2>Gold Mining Equipment for Tanzania</h2>
      <p>Tanzania is Africa's fourth-largest gold producer, with active alluvial and small-scale mining across the Lake Victoria Goldfield and the southern Lupa belt. Our wash plants are container-ready for shipping into Dar es Salaam and engineered for the lateritic soils, tropical rainfall, and remote site conditions typical of Tanzanian artisanal and small-scale (ASM) operations.</p>
      <h3>Why Tanzanian Miners Choose Us</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Container-ready for shipping into Dar es Salaam, onward to Mwanza and the goldfield</li>
        <li>Mercury-free — meets Tanzania Minerals Commission and Minamata Convention standards</li>
        <li>Built for the lateritic and weathered greenstone deposits of the Lake Victoria region</li>
        <li>Handles tropical clay, monsoon conditions, and seasonal river flow</li>
        <li>Simple operation — ideal for ASM crews with limited prior heavy-equipment experience</li>
        <li>30-minute setup gets crews recovering gold the day equipment arrives on site</li>
      </ul>
      <p>From the artisanal operations around Geita and Mwanza to the larger licensed concessions in the Lupa Goldfield, our equipment recovers fine gold from deposits where traditional sluice methods leave money in the tailings. <a href="/contact/">Contact us for Tanzania pricing and shipping quotes</a>.</p>
